report.body:
Version: curl 8.23.0

The function `imap_state_login_resp()` in lib/imap.c at line 1912 does not validate its input length before use.

```c
static CURLcode imap_state_login_resp(struct Curl_easy *data,
                                      struct imap_conn *imapc,
                                      int imapcode,
                                      imapstate instate)
{
  CURLcode result = CURLE_OK;
  (void)instate;

  if(imapcode != IMAP_RESP_OK) {
    failf(data, "Access denied. %c", imapcode);
    result = CURLE_LOGIN_DENIED;
  }
```

This can lead to memory corruption with a malicious server.

